Declare the asset folder:

yaml
flutter:
  uses-material-design: true
  assets:
    - assets/gifs/
Also add assets/gifs/.gitkeep (or a placeholder GIF) so the asset folder isn't empty — an empty declared asset directory causes a build error.

Notification init: call flutterLocalNotificationsPlugin.initialize(...) in main() before runApp, and configure the timezone database (tz.initializeTimeZones() + set local location). Request POST_NOTIFICATIONS at first launch of the app via a permission gate, not on every start.

Battery optimization / exact alarms: On Android 12+, exact alarms require the user to grant SCHEDULE_EXACT_ALARM. Handle gracefully — if not granted, fall back to inexact scheduling.

UX / POLISH REQUIREMENTS
Material 3 (useMaterial3: true), with a fitness-appropriate color seed (e.g. a teal/green "hydro" accent).

All empty states must have a message + illustration/icon + action button (e.g. "No workouts scheduled yet — tap + to add one").

All loading/error states handled (DB init failure, permission denied).

No hardcoded magic strings in UI — centralize in a strings.dart or use constants.

Consistent spacing/padding, rounded corners, subtle elevation on cards.

The timer modal must have a visible "Cancel training" action that cancels the timer and its scheduled fallback notification.

Accessibility: semantic labels on interactive elements, sufficient contrast, minimum 48dp touch targets.

DELIVERABLES FROM THE AGENT
The agent should produce, in order:

Scaffolding: flutter create hydrofit, update pubspec.yaml, run flutter pub get, and confirm no analyzer errors.

Data layer: models, seed data (40+ exercises, 25+ meals), SQLite helper, repositories.

Services: notification service (with timezone + permission handling + resync), timer service.

Providers for theme, schedule, and notification settings.

Screens in this order: Home (bottom nav shell) → Training → Diet → Schedule → Account.

Android config (manifest, gradle desugaring) applied early — the agent should do this before writing the notification service so it doesn't forget.

A placeholder GIF in assets/gifs/test.gif (generate a tiny one or instruct the user to drop one in) to verify asset loading before the user downloads the full library.

README at project root documenting: how to run, how to add new exercises/meals, how to name GIF files, and any known Android quirks.

Final verification: run flutter analyze and flutter build apk --debug and resolve all errors before declaring done. Do not stop at "code written" — the app must build.

CONSTRAINTS & NON-GOALS
Do not add Firebase, Supabase, any cloud SDK, or analytics.

Do not add authentication UI or logic.

Do not target iOS, web, or desktop.

Do not add video player packages (e.g. youtube_player_flutter) — use url_launcher only.

Do not introduce state management beyond provider.

Do not generate large binary assets (GIFs, videos) — use placeholders and instruct the user to populate assets/gifs/.

HOW TO WORK THROUGH THIS
Work feature-by-feature in the order listed above. After each feature, run flutter analyze, fix all issues, and confirm the app still builds. Ask the user for clarification only if a requirement is genuinely ambiguous — otherwise make reasonable decisions and document them in the README. At the end, present a summary of what was built, what the user must do next (add real GIFs, test on device, grant notification permission), and any known limitations.
